pokebw2-sdk.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): pokebw2's C against libntr's and libntrsystem's headers in
place of pokebw2's lib/nitro and lib/nnsys ones. The restatements of SDK inlines pokebw2's headers lack (PAD_Read,
MATH_IMin, the display-control readers, NNS_G3dGetTexDataByIdx) are left to libntr's under SDK_PORT (libntr's
define); libntr's member names (NNSG2dMultiCellHierarchyData's posX/posY, MtxFx43's _30.._32, FSOverlayInfo's header,
OSTWLParentalControl's flags, the file header's sigVal, the joint animation's tags after the struct); OVERLAY_ID as the
overlay's number (an address is no u32 constant initializer on a 64-bit host, Black's include/gfl/overlay.h);
gf_overlay.c's ranges as uintptr_t; arc_tool.c's one assembly function (pokebw2's last non-matching function, which
clang cannot build) as the C of Black's port (lib/gfl/src/arc_tool.c).

diff --git a/include/gfl/overlay.h b/include/gfl/overlay.h
index 873165368..bb0239676 100644
--- a/include/gfl/overlay.h
+++ b/include/gfl/overlay.h
@@ -5,7 +5,11 @@
 #include "gfl/heap.h"
 
 // The linker script defines OVERLAY_<n>_ID for every overlay, so that overlay IDs in the code are relocations
+#ifdef SDK_PORT   // (the port: the overlay's number; an address is no u32 constant initializer on a 64-bit host)
+#define OVERLAY_ID(n) ((u32)(n))
+#else
 #define OVERLAY_ID(n) ((u32)OVERLAY_##n##_ID)
+#endif
 // For procs in the main program, which need no overlay
 #define OVERLAY_NONE (-1)
 
